 "ばあいわけ": "مَجْمُوعَة, جَمَاعَة (A number of things or persons being in some relation to one another.)  [grouping]",
 "ばあさん": "جَدَّة (A mother of someone's parent.)  [grandmother]\nusu. 祖母さん\nمثال: 今日は、ばーさんのお使いを兼ねて街で買い物。\n→ Today I'm shopping in town as well as running an errand for my grandmother. / عَجُوز (An elderly woman.)  [old woman]\n婆さん\nمثال: 「店のばーさんは、すげー愛想悪いんだけどさー」「大輝、聞こえとるぞ」「げっ・・・」\n→ \"The old lady of this shop is very unsociable but ...\" \"Taiki, I can hear you!\" \"Ack!\"",
 "ばあちゃん": "جِدَّة (colloquial: grandmother — see also grandma) / تِيتَة (colloquial: grandmother — see also grandma)  [granny] / عَجُوز (An elderly woman.)  [old woman]",
 "ばあば": "جَدَّة, تِيتَة (Grandmother.)  [grandma]",
 "ばあや": "[elderly housekeeper ; elderly maid]\nalso vocative / ظِئْر, دَايَة (A woman hired to suckle and care for another woman's child.)  [wet nurse]",
 "ばい": "ثُنَائِيّ (Made up of two matching or complementary elements.) / ضِعْف (Of twice the quantity.)  [double]\nمثال: 彼は私の倍食べた。\n→ He ate twice as much as I did. / فِي (Multiplied by (see also 'ratio of comparison' sense at 'time').)  [times (as much)]\nمثال: あの山はこの山の５倍の高さである。\n→ That mountain is five times as high as this one. / [1-nth ; 1 to n]\ne.g. 40倍 = 1 in 40",
