 "ばかり": "وَحِيد (1. alone in a category) / فَقَط (Without others or anything further; exclusively.) / فَقَط (No more than; just.) / فَقَط (Introduces a clause with negative polarity, often one which upsets the listener')  [only]\nمثال: ５０００円ばかりもっている。\n→ I have about 5,000 yen. / حَوَالَيْ, تَقْرِيبًا (Imprecise but close to in quantity or amount.)  [approximately]\nمثال: あなたの妹はいつも自分の夫のことで文句ばかり言っている。\n→ That sister of yours is always complaining of her husband. / عَدْل (Morally right; upright, righteous, equitable; fair.) / فَقَط (only, simply, merely)  [just (finished, etc.)]\nafter the -ta form of a verb\nمثال: 「君はそれを終えたか」「とんでもない、始めたばかりだ」\n→ \"Have you finished it?\" \"On the contrary, I've just begun.\" / عَلَى وَشْك (Indicates that one is preparing or planning to do the stated thing at some time )  [(as though) about to]\nafter an attributive form or auxiliary verb ぬ(ん), also often …とばかり(に)",
