 "ひきだし": "جَارُور, دُرْج (An open-topped box that can be slid in and out of the cabinet that contains it, ) / رَسَّام, رَسَّامَة (An artist who primarily makes drawings.)  [drawer]\nمثال: きれいなタオルは引き出しにありますよ。\n→ The clean towels are in the drawer. / اِنْسِحَاب (An act of withdrawing or a state of being withdrawn.)  [withdrawal (of money from an account)] / [variety of knowledge and experience useful for handling things impromptu]",
 "ひきだす": "عَزَلَ (To use coitus interruptus as a method of birth control.)  [to pull out]\nمثال: 私は封筒を開けて手紙を引き出した。\n→ I opened the envelope and pulled out a letter. / يَسْتَحْضِر, يَسْتَدْعِي (To ask someone to come; to send for.)  [to summon (e.g. to court)] / سَحَبَ (To extract (money) from a bank account or other financial deposit.) / تَرَاجَعَ (Chiefly followed by from: to leave a place, someone's presence, etc., to go to a)  [to withdraw (money)]\nمثال: 太郎は銀行から一万円引き出した。\n→ Taro drew 10,000 yen from the bank. / مُقْتَطَف (A portion of a book, document, recording etc. incorporated distinctly in another) / خلاصة (A decoction, solution, or infusion made by drawing out from any substance that w)  [to extract (information, the truth, etc.)]\nمثال: 彼はその調査から結論を引き出した。\n→ He drew his conclusions based on that survey.",
