 "ひつようははつめいのはは": "اَلْحَاجَة أَمّ اَلاِخْتِرَاع (The primary driving force for most new inventions is a need.)  [necessity is the mother of invention]",
 "ひつようひん": "ضَرُورَة, حَاجَة (The quality or state of being necessary, unavoidable, or absolutely requisite.)  [necessities]",
 "ひつようふかけつ": "حَيَوِيّ (Relating to or characteristic of life.) / أَسَاسِيّ (Necessary to the continuation of life; being the seat of life; being that on whi)  [vital]\nمثال: 水は生命に必要不可欠です。\n→ Water is indispensable to life.",
