 "ひょうめん": "سَطْح (The overside or upside of a flat object such as a table, or of a liquid.) / سَطْح (The locus of an equation (especially one with exactly two degrees of freedom) in) / طفا إلى السطح (To rise to the surface.) / طفا إلى السطح (To become known or apparent; to appear or be found; to come to light.)  [surface]\nمثال: 突然の風で池の表面が波立った。\n→ A sudden wind agitated the surface of the pond. / خَارِج, بره (The part of something that faces out; the outer surface.) / خَارِج (Outdoors.) / خَارِج (On the outside of, not inside (something, such as a building).)  [outside] / ظُهُور (The act of appearing or coming into sight; the act of becoming visible to the ey) / مَظْهَر (A thing seen; a phenomenon; an apparition.) / مَظْهَر, شَكْل (The way something looks; personal presence) / شَكْل (Apparent likeness; the way which something or someone appears to others.)  [appearances]",
 "ひょうめんか": "اِنْكَسَرَ (intransitive: to separate into (to end up in) two or more pi) / كَسَرَ (transitive: to separate into (to cause to end up in) two or ) / اِسْتِرَاحَة (rest or pause, usually from work)  [breaking]",
 "ひょうめんかこう": "وَجْه, مُحَيًّا (The front part of the head of a human or other animal, featuring the eyes, nose,) / مَظْهَر (Public image; outward appearance.) / وَاجَهَ (To deal with (a difficult situation or person); to accept (facts, reality, etc.))  [facing]",
 "ひょうめんかっせいざい": "عَامِل سَطْحِيّ (A surface-active agent, or wetting agent, capable of reducing the surface tensio)  [surfactant]",
 "ひょうめんじょう": "فِي مَا يَبْدُو, عَلَى مَا يَبْدُو (Seemingly, apparently, on the surface; supposedly, according to representations )  [ostensibly]\nمثال: 表面上、本書の大部分は一連の事例の変遷を記録したものである。\n→ On the surface the book consists mostly of a series of case histories.",
 "ひょうめんてき": "سَطْحِيّ (Not thorough, deep, or complete; concerned only with the obvious or apparent.)  [superficial]\nمثال: それらの間には表面的な相違はない。\n→ There is no surface difference between them.",
 "ひょうりいったい": "وَجْهَانِ لِعُمْلَةٍ وَاحِدَةٍ (Two aspects of the same thing.)  [two sides of the same coin]",
 "ひょうりょう": "وَزْن (The process by which something is weighed.)  [weighing] / [maximum weight (on a scale)]",
 "ひょうりん": "قَمَر, قمر (Any natural satellite of a planet.)  [the moon]",
 "ひょうれい": "[fluttering to the ground (of a leaf or petal)] / تَجَوَّلَ (To move without purpose or specified destination; often in search of livelihood.)  [wandering] / [coming down in the world ; going to ruin]",
 "ひょうろう": "طَعَام, أَكْل (Any solid substance that can be consumed by living organisms, especially by eati)  [food]",
 "ひょうろくだま": "مُغَفَّل, سَاذَج (A simple-minded person lacking common sense.)  [simpleton]",
 "ひょうろく玉": "مُغَفَّل, سَاذَج (A simple-minded person lacking common sense.)  [simpleton]",
 "ひょうろん": "نَقْد, اِنْتِقَاد (The act of criticising; a critical judgment passed or expressed.)  [criticism]\nمثال: 芸術家は時には評論を軽蔑することがある。\n→ Some artists are contemptuous of criticism.",
 "ひょうろんか": "نَقَّاد, نَاقِد (A person who appraises the works of others.) / ناقد (One who criticizes; a person who finds fault.)  [critic]\nمثال: あらゆる芸術評論家達は無能であり危険な存在である。\n→ Regard all art critics as useless and dangerous.",
 "ひょう疽": "دَاحِس (Inflammation and/or infection in the cuticle and/or the nailbed of a fingernail )  [whitlow]",
 "ひょこっと": "فَجْأَةً (Happening quickly and with little or no warning; in a sudden manner.)  [suddenly]",
 "ひょっくり": "فَجْأَةً (Suddenly, quickly, without warning.)  [all of a sudden]\nمثال: あなたにここでひょっこり出会えてうれしい。\n→ I am glad to run into you here.",
 "ひょっこり": "فَجْأَةً (Suddenly, quickly, without warning.)  [all of a sudden]\nمثال: あなたにここでひょっこり出会えてうれしい。\n→ I am glad to run into you here.",
 "ひょっと": "رُبَّمَا (indicating a lack of certainty) / مِن اَلْمُمْكِن (indicating a lack of certainty) / لَعَلَّ (indicating a lack of certainty)  [perhaps] / عَنْ غَفْلَةٍ (Without meaning to, in an unintentional manner, not intentionally.)  [unintentionally]",
 "ひょっとこ": "[Hyottoko ; comical male character with puckered, skewed mouth] / مُهَرِّج (A slapstick performance artist often associated with a circus and usually charac) / مُهَرِّج (A person who acts in a silly fashion.)  [clown]",
 "ひょっとしたら": "رُبَّمَا (indicating a lack of certainty) / مِن اَلْمُمْكِن (indicating a lack of certainty) / لَعَلَّ (indicating a lack of certainty)  [perhaps]\nمثال: 彼の予言は、ひょっとしたら的中するかもしれない。\n→ His prediction might come true.",
 "ひょっとすると": "رُبَّمَا (indicating a lack of certainty) / مِن اَلْمُمْكِن (indicating a lack of certainty) / لَعَلَّ (indicating a lack of certainty)  [perhaps]\nمثال: ひょっとすると明日は雨かもしれない。\n→ Perhaps it will rain tomorrow.",
 "ひょろい": "ضَعِيف (Lacking in force (usually strength) or ability.) / ضَعِيف (Dilute, lacking in taste or potency.)  [weak]",
 "ひょろける": "تَرَنُّح (An unsteady movement of the body in walking or standing as if one were about to ) / تَرَنَّحَ (To sway unsteadily, reel, or totter.)  [to stagger]",
 "ひょろつく": "تَرَنُّح (An unsteady movement of the body in walking or standing as if one were about to ) / تَرَنَّحَ (To sway unsteadily, reel, or totter.)  [to stagger]",
 "ひょろひょろ": "[totteringly ; staggeringly] / نَحِيف, أَهْيَف (To attenuate.)  [slender]",
 "ひょんな": "غَرِيب, عَجِيب (Not normal; odd, unusual, surprising, out of the ordinary, often with a negative) / أَجْنَبِيّ, غَرِيب (Unfamiliar, not yet part of one's experience.)  [strange]\nمثال: 昨日、ひょんなことで父親の戸籍抄本のコピーを見てしまいました。\n→ Yesterday I stumbled across a copy of my father's family register.",
 "ひょんなことから": "صُدْفَةً, بِصُدْفَة (Unexpectedly, accidentally; without foreplanning.)  [by chance]",
 "ひょんな事から": "صُدْفَةً, بِصُدْفَة (Unexpectedly, accidentally; without foreplanning.)  [by chance]",
 "ひよう": "سَاوَى, كَلَّفَ (To incur a charge of; to require payment of a (specified) price.) / تَكْلِفَة, كُلْفَة (Amount of money, time, etc. that is required or used.)  [cost]\nمثال: 諸設備の費用は払っていただきます。\n→ You have to pay for utilities.",
 "ひようしゃ": "مُوَظَّف, مُوَظَّفَة (A person who provides labor to a company or another person.)  [employee]",
 "ひようとり": "مُياوِم (A laborer who is hired and paid one day at a time, with no promise that more wor)  [day laborer]",
 "ひよく": "خَصِب (Of land, etc.: capable of growing abundant crops; productive.) / خَصِب (Capable of reproducing; fecund, fruitful.)  [fertile]\nمثال: 肥沃な土壌は豊かな作物を産する。\n→ Rich soil yields good crops.",
 "ひよくなみかづきちたい": "الهِلَال الخَصِيب (A crescent-shaped geographic region of fertile land in the Middle East in Wester)  [Fertile Crescent]",
 "ひよけ": "مَظَلَّة (Something to keep the sun off, or create shade from the sun; a parasol or awning)  [sunshade]\nمثال: 歩道の上には日よけがあった。\n→ There was a sunshade over the sidewalk. / مَظَلَّة, شَمْسِيَّة (A small light umbrella used as protection from the sun.)  [parasol]",
 "ひよこ": "صُوص, فَرُّوج (A young bird.) / فَتَاة (An attractive, young woman; or, more generally, a woman.)  [chick]\nمثال: ヒヨコが餌を探して地面をつついている。\n→ The chickens were scratching for food on the ground. / [greenhorn ; fledgeling]\nمثال: ルチアーノは大声援を背負って戦えるかもしれないが、彼はまだヒヨコに過ぎない。\n→ Luciano might have the crowd behind him, but he's still wet behind the ears.",
 "ひよこまめ": "حِمِّص (A seed of this plant, often used as a food.)  [chickpea (Cicer arietinum)]",
