 "ひよっこ": "صُوص, فَرُّوج (A young bird.) / فَتَاة (An attractive, young woman; or, more generally, a woman.)  [chick]\nمثال: ヒヨコが餌を探して地面をつついている。\n→ The chickens were scratching for food on the ground. / [greenhorn ; fledgeling]\nمثال: ルチアーノは大声援を背負って戦えるかもしれないが、彼はまだヒヨコに過ぎない。\n→ Luciano might have the crowd behind him, but he's still wet behind the ears.",
 "ひより": "طَقْس, جَوّ (The short-term state of the atmosphere at a specific time and place, including t)  [weather] / [fine weather ; clear day] / حَالَة, وَضْع (The combination of circumstances at a given moment; a state of affairs.) / حَالَة, وَضْع (The way in which something is positioned vis-à-vis its surroundings.) / حَالَة, وَضْع (The place in which something is situated; a location.) / حَالَة, وَضْع (Position or status with regard to conditions and circumstances.)  [situation] / [sea conditions ; good day for sailing]",
 "ひよりみ": "اِمْتَطَى (To sit or stand with a leg on each side of something; to sit astride.)  [straddling]\nمثال: ひより見をする。\n→ See which way the cat jumps.",
 "ひよわ": "ضَعِيف (Lacking in force (usually strength) or ability.) / ضَعِيف (Dilute, lacking in taste or potency.)  [weak]\nمثال: 彼はあまりにもひ弱で戸外でゲームをする事はなかった。\n→ He was too frail to play games outdoors.",
