 "ふりおとす": "اِنْتَفَضَ (To remove (something attached to, on or clinging to an object) by shaking.)  [to shake off]",
 "ふりかえ": "حَوَّلَ (To move or pass from one place, person or thing to another.) / اِنْتِقَال (act)  [transfer]\nمثال: ですから私たちは、社員が現金ではなく、エレクトロニクスによる振替でお金を受け取るよう、説得に努めているのです。\n→ Therefore, we try to persuade people not to have cash, to have money electronically transferred. / [money transfer (usu. between accounts held by the same person)] / [postal transfer]",
 "ふりかえゆそう": "حَوَّلَ (To move or pass from one place, person or thing to another.) / اِنْتِقَال (act)  [transfer (of passengers or freight)] / [substitute transportation ; alternative transportation]",
 "ふりかえる": "تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [to change (e.g. a bill)]",
 "ふりかかる": "وَقَعَ, سَقَطَ (To be moved downwards.) / سَقَطَ (To happen; to come to pass; to chance or light (upon).) / سُقُوط, هُوِيّ (The act of moving to a lower position under the effect of gravity.)  [to fall (on)] / حَدَثَ, جَرَى (To occur or take place.)  [to happen (to)]\nمثال: 途中で何かが彼の身に降りかかったに違いない。\n→ Something must have happened to him on the way.",
