 "ふりたてる": "لَوَّحَ, رَفْرَفَ (To move one's hand back and forth (generally above the shoulders) in greeting or) / مَوْج, مَوْجَة (A moving disturbance in the level of a body of liquid; an undulation.)  [to wave (i.e. a flag)]",
 "ふりだし": "[shaking (something) out] / بِدَايَة (The act of doing that which begins anything; commencement of an action, state, o) / بِدَايَة (That which begins or originates something; the source or first cause.) / بِدَايَة (The initial portion of some extended thing.)  [beginning]\nمثال: 振り出しに戻ってしまった。\n→ We were back to square one. / رَسْم (A picture, likeness, diagram or representation, usually drawn on paper.) / رَسْم (The act of producing such a picture.)  [drawing (e.g. of a bill)] / رَمَى, صَبَّ (To cause a certain number on the die or dice to be shown after rolling it.)  [throw (of dice)]",
 "ふりだす": "[to shake out]\nمثال: フェンスの向こう側に片足を振り出した。\n→ I swung my leg over the fence. / عَدَد (Someone or something that flows out or comes out) / مُشْكِل, مَسْأَلَة (Any question or situation to be resolved)  [to issue (e.g. money order)] / [to infuse (e.g. in hot water)]\nمثال: 小切手はＡＢＣ社あてに支払われるように振り出してください。\n→ Checks should be made payable to the ABC Company.",
